        <h1>The Liminal Space of Sleep: <span class="pop">What Happens to Your Brain in the Seconds Before You Fall Asleep</span></h1>
        <p class="post-meta">
          <time datetime={publishDate}>5 June 2026</time> &#183; 11 min read
        </p>
        <p class="article-intro">
          Everyone is talking about liminal spaces right now &#8212; those eerie, uncanny in-between places. But there is a liminal space you visit every single night: hypnagogia, the threshold between waking and sleeping. It has a name, a neuroscience, and a frequency signature. And The Sleep Math is built on exactly those numbers.
        </p>
      </header>

      <img
        class="hero-img"
